# RUN: llc -mtriple=haydn-unknown-elf -global-isel-abort=1 \
# RUN:     -run-pass=instruction-select -verify-machineinstrs %s -o - \
# RUN:     | FileCheck %s

# Role: MIR — once-per-MF bank-aware pre-constrain of bank-only vregs
# (GOALS W45, PA2-B5).

# REGRESSION TEST: preConstrainBankOnlyVRegs mapped EVERY 64-bit bank-only
# vreg to DR64RegClass and ran per-MI (O(N_vregs x N_instrs)).
#
# Bug: ARRegBank does not cover DR64RegClass, so the blanket 64-bit->DR64
# constrain SILENTLY FAILED for an AR-banked 64-bit vreg (the return of
# constrainGenericRegister was dropped) and left the vreg bank-only. The
# first COPY touching it then died with "cannot select" (observed:
# "LLVM ERROR: cannot select: $ar0 = COPY %1:arregbank(s64)"). The COPY
# early path had the same mis-bank: it tested DR64/size-64 BEFORE the AR
# bank, so a 64-bit AR-banked operand mis-banked to DR64 there too (W36
# residual note).
#
# Fix: the walk is hoisted to once per MachineFunction (selector setupMF,
# AArch64/RISCV peer shape) and the class choice is bank-aware in ONE rule
# (bankAwareRegClass): existing class wins; 64-bit AR-banked -> ARRegClass;
# else size default (64 -> DR64, else GPR32). ARRegClass is
# isAllocatable=0, so it is entered via MRI::setRegClassOrRegBank (the one
# constraint entry without an allocatability check — W36 precedent).
#
# Test design: one mixed function carries a GPR32-banked s32, a DR64-banked
# s64, and an AR-banked s64; each is produced by G_IMPLICIT_DEF (the MIR
# runs -verify-machineinstrs, and an incoming physreg like $r1 would be
# "undefined physical register" — there is no live-in/CallLowering here) and
# each flows to a same-bank physreg COPY. AR banked vregs cannot be produced
# by the IR pipeline today (AR is pinned as physregs by the AGU intrinsic
# selectors and MIR rejects class:ar — see ar-unallocatable-class.mir), so
# MIR with class:arregbank is the one legal entry that drives the latent
# surface, exactly like HaydnRegisterBankInfoTest.cpp drives getInstrMapping.
#
# What breaks if the bug returns: %2 (AR-banked s64) prints class
# "arregbank" (bank-only, constrain silently dropped) and llc aborts with
# "cannot select" on the $ar0 COPY before any CHECK matches.

# CHECK-LABEL: name: mixed_dr64_ar_gpr32
# CHECK: registers:
# CHECK-NEXT:   - { id: 0, class: gpr32,
# CHECK: class: dr64,
# CHECK: class: ar,
# CHECK: IMPLICIT_DEF
# CHECK: $d0 = COPY %1
# CHECK: $ar0 = COPY %2
# CHECK: $r2 = COPY %0
# CHECK: RET

--- |
  define void @mixed_dr64_ar_gpr32() { ret void }
...
---
name: mixed_dr64_ar_gpr32
legalized: true
regBankSelected: true
tracksRegLiveness: true
registers:
  - { id: 0, class: gpr32regbank }
  - { id: 1, class: dr64regbank }
  - { id: 2, class: arregbank }
body:             |
  bb.0:
    %0:gpr32regbank(s32) = G_IMPLICIT_DEF
    %1:dr64regbank(s64) = G_IMPLICIT_DEF
    %2:arregbank(s64) = G_IMPLICIT_DEF
    $d0 = COPY %1(s64)
    $ar0 = COPY %2(s64)
    $r2 = COPY %0(s32)
    RET implicit $r15
...
